WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.150
- I so often hear people send the message

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.370
like thank God that's not me when they see

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.770
someone with a disability or like

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.480
thank God that's not me or my kid.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.000
And that's sending the message that

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.310
disability is equal to
someone who is less than

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.151
or broken or incomplete
and that's not the case.

00:00:15.151 --> 00:00:17.734
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.533
- I have Cerebral Palsy.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.960
It affects me pretty
much from the hips down

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.890
and also just like fine motor
control and things like that.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.840
- So I have Tourette Syndrome which is

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.260
a neurological disorder which means I do

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.350
movements and noises that I can't control.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.260
- I have Cerebral Palsy
as well left Hemiparesis

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.330
and Nystagmus which means that my whole

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.860
left side is weaker than my rights.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.710
- I have a very aggressive form for Lupus.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.210
And I have a blood clotting
disorder associated

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:54.038
with my Lupus and four years
ago I had a clot in my foot.

00:00:54.038 --> 00:00:56.210
And then this happened
and over eight months

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.793
and 11 surgeries, this was the end.

00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:01.536
(upbeat music)

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.513
- I...

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.200
love having Tourette's.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.633
I love that I'm four foot, seven.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.259
I love my obsessive compulsive disorder.

00:01:10.259 --> 00:01:12.630
And I think that's the
case that many of us

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.900
have embraced our disabilities.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.380
- I've had my disabilities
since I was born

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.233
and it's a part me.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:24.850
- My brain is quick and witty
and wildly inappropriate.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.960
And it also has Tourette's
and at some point

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.523
I decided not to just
love parts of my brain.

00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:32.630
(upbeat music)

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.798
A lot of times I see kids staring at me.

00:01:35.798 --> 00:01:37.320
That's OK with me.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.613
- I welcome it, kids are curious.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.610
- But what I struggle
with is when a parent

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.152
shushes them or quickly pulls
them in the other direction.

00:01:44.152 --> 00:01:48.250
- When a child is hustled
away from a person

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.683
or hushed, it stigmatizes
even just asking the question.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.180
- Because kids then associate disability

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.490
with feeling ashamed.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.890
- If they've never seen
anything like this before

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.030
they're gonna look and if
they questions let them ask.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.340
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.640
- So instead I hope that
parents say things like:

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.790
How cool that we all move differently

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.810
and walk differently and talk differently.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.600
More than just like normalizing disability

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.833
but celebrating it.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.130
We date, people with disabilities date!

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.879
And not always other
people with disabilities.

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:20.550
- Just because I have I disability doesn't

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.320
mean I have to be paired with
somebody with a disability.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.560
- Direct message to everyone in my life

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.390
but if you're gonna set
me up on a blind date

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.124
please have more criteria than

00:02:29.124 --> 00:02:31.423
this guy also has a disability.

00:02:31.898 --> 00:02:34.120
(upbeat music)

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.790
- Not every single
person with a disability

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:37.823
is in a wheelchair.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.320
I am not in a wheelchair.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.993
I've never been in a wheelchair.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.650
(upbeat music)

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.270
- If one more person
calls me an inspiration

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.253
after just meeting me, I'm
gonna burn your house down.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.010
- We aren't inherently
inspirational or brave

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.450
because we are disabled.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.400
We're just kind of the idea that people

00:02:55.421 --> 00:02:57.221
think about what when they say that.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.400
- It's OK to call me an
inspiration once you know me.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.763
Or know something about me.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.060
But genetics does not
make me an inspiration.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.140
Let me earn that word.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.880
- There are people who are actually doing

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.083
amazing, brave things out there.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.253
Whether they have a disability or not.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.263
- But it comes across
to a disabled person as:

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.623
wow I'm so happy that
I'm not in your shoes.

00:03:17.826 --> 00:03:19.360
(upbeat music)

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.908
- I get a lot of strangers
trying to help me.

00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:26.770
Up the steps by grabbing my
arm or my waste or something.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.460
And that's extremely inappropriate.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.410
- You can say hey do you need some help?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.263
Rather than just either forcing
my chair or ignoring me.

00:03:34.716 --> 00:03:37.299
(upbeat music)

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.720
It took me awhile to actually call myself

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.160
a person with a disability.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.430
But I'm a person first.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.223
Being an amputee is secondary.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.900
- I rather have somebody say
I'm a person with a disability

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.717
rather than being disabled because of the

00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:53.380
whole control and ownership issue.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.763
- I hear differently abled.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.760
The word is disability.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.680
- They used to call myself
like differently abled

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.890
and some people didn't like that.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.250
And I'm just like, but I am different

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.200
and their like no you're not

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.050
and it took me awhile to actually see

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.550
that I was using very able-bodied terms.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:10.760
- It should be a descriptor.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.623
Just like I'm right-handed,
I have a disability.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.020
(upbeat music)

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.743
When we're talking about
disabilities I hear

00:04:17.743 --> 00:04:20.840
the word that we wanna be
accommodating, which is great.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.190
Or we're working on tolerance.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.850
Nobody wants to just be tolerated.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.250
Like I tolerated those
three years my sister

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.720
was learning to play the trombone.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.513
I tolerate going to the dentist.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.790
None of these things are things I like,

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:32.930
they're things I tolerate

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.450
because I know that I have to deal with.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.260
So there's such an important
step in communities

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.520
between opening the door to
somebody with a disability

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.235
and like embracing them

00:04:41.235 --> 00:04:43.603
and building a community
with them in mind.

00:04:43.861 --> 00:04:46.444
(upbeat music)

